# Solved environment. `pixi.lock` IS committed so a runner reproduces the
# exact solve; the materialised environment is not.
.pixi/

# `mojo precompile` output for the `build-pkg` task. The task does `mkdir -p`
# because precompile will not create its own output directory and fails with
# "cannot open output file" on a clean clone otherwise.
build/

# Python bytecode from the bench harness. `bench/` and `tools/` hold scripts
# that the pixi bench and skgpu environments import, so running them leaves
# these behind.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# `mojo build` output written next to the source rather than into build/.
# These are native binaries for whichever chip built them; committing one
# would ship a Mac-only artifact into a repository that claims portability.
/kmeans_main
/knn_main
/probe_main
/oracle_main
/matrix_main
/vendor_main

# The tokenizer's Unicode class table, generated at build time from Python's
# unicodedata by tokenizer/tools/gen_unicode_table.sh (2026-09-15). No data
# file is tracked; the pin is in tokenizer/impl/unicode_class.mojo.
tokenizer/impl/unicode_table_generated.mojo

# Agent worktrees: transient, and each is its own git repo
.claude/worktrees/

# the upper tiers' binary sets (MOJOLEARN_NUMERIC_MODE=<tier> bash bindings/build_*.sh);
# built per machine, never committed. `deterministic/` joined its sibling here on
# 2026-08-29 -- until it did, the new tier's artifacts made the tree DIRTY and the
# remote leg refused to rent, which is the dirty-tree guard working on a directory
# that had simply never been listed.
python/mojolearn/identical/
python/mojolearn/deterministic/

# E1/E2/E3 leg artifacts: the saved models are reproducible from the cells (tools/e1_traced_fit.py, e2_matrix_fit.py) and are not committed
bench/results/e1/*/*.model.npz
bench/results/e1/*/control/
bench/results/e1/.leg-*.state

# CatBoost writes this training-log directory beside whatever invoked it.
# Regenerated on every run, never an input to anything here.
catboost_info/

# NOTE: -dirty ladder runs are DELIBERATELY TRACKED records (see gemm/ DEVIATION 533).
# They are not junk and must not be ignored or removed.
# Dry-run leg output is not a record.
bench/results/e1g/*-dryrun/

# the Linux wheel legs' fetched binary sets (packaging/linux/leg.sh). The
# manifests, sizes, gate JSON and logs beside them ARE committed; the
# binaries and the packed wheels are build outputs of a rented box.
bench/results/wheels/*/wheels/sets/*/
bench/results/wheels/*/wheels/sets/*.tar.gz
bench/results/wheels/*/wheels/tools-venv/
# The SAME files under their raw fetch path. `leg.sh` copies `diag/` out of
# bench/results/e1/<stamp>-<vendor>/ into bench/results/wheels/<stamp>-<vendor>/,
# so everything here is a second copy, and the rules above matched only the
# copy. A 15.8 MB `cuda.tar.gz` was staged for commit on 2026-08-30 through
# this gap.
bench/results/e1/*/diag/wheels/sets/*/
bench/results/e1/*/diag/wheels/sets/*.tar.gz
bench/results/e1/*/diag/wheels/tools-venv/

# macOS Finder metadata. Never content.
.DS_Store

# BUILD ARTIFACTS AND RAW DUMPS UNDER bench/, UNTRACKED 2026-08-31.
#
# They were 235 files and 333 MB against an EVIDENCE BASE OF 5.5 MB. The
# cards, the verdict markdown, the hashes and the maps are what back a claim;
# a compiled .so, a fetched binary set and a raw tensor dump back nothing and
# can be regenerated. They are still written and still read locally; they are
# simply not carried in the repository, where they made the tree 18,346 files
# and every AMD leg lose eleven minutes of a sixty-minute lease to scp.
bench/**/*.bin
bench/**/*.so
bench/**/*.tar.gz
# bootstrap.log IS NOT IGNORED, and the attempt to ignore it is why this
# comment exists. It looked like 59 MB of compiler warnings. E1U_RESULTS.md:72
# cites a COUNT out of it, and E1_RESULTS.md:71 and E2_RESULTS.md:126 list it
# by name as part of the evidence bundle. Six documents reference it. An
# artifact a result cites is evidence, whatever its signal-to-noise ratio.

# 2026-09-08: bytes that are never evidence and once blocked every push for a
# day (a 119 MB artifacts.tar over GitHub's 100 MiB limit). Wheels live on
# PyPI, tarballs are packed copies of files beside them, fixture dumps are
# regenerable from the Mojo driver. tools/hooks/pre-commit refuses them too.
bench/results/**/*.whl
bench/results/**/*.tar
bench/results/**/*.tar.gz
bench/results/**/*.tgz
bench/results/**/*.fixture
bench/results/**/remote/dump/

# A release leg fetches the pod's patchelf venv beside its evidence; a
# venv is a tool, not evidence (2026-09-10, five legs x 800 files).
bench/results/e1g/*/remote/tools-venv/

